[Event "French: Advance"]

{The French (1...e6 2...d5) concedes space but builds a solid chain. Black's plan is always to attack the base of White's chain with ...c5 and ...f6.}
1. e4 {Claims the centre: the pawn on e4 controls d5 and f5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1 and the bishop on f1.}
1... e6 {[%csl Gd5] The French: prepares ...d5. Supports the centre: the pawn on e6 controls d5 and f5. It also opens a line for the queen on d8 and the bishop on f8.}
2. d4 {Builds a centre. The pawn on d4 controls c5 and e5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1 and the queen on d1.}
2... d5 {[%cal Gd5e4] Challenges e4. Claims the centre: the pawn on d5 controls c4 and eyes the pawn on e4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
3. e5 {The Advance: gains space. Claims the centre: the pawn on e5 controls d6 and f6.}
3... c5 {[%cal Gc5d4] Attacks the base of the chain. Supports the centre: the pawn on c5 controls b4 and eyes the pawn on d4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
4. c3 {Supports d4. Supports the centre: the pawn on c3 controls b4 and supports the pawn on d4. It also opens a line for the queen on d1.}
4... Nc6 {More pressure on d4. Develops the knight to c6, where it eyes the pawn on d4 and the pawn on e5.}
5. Nf3 {Supports d4. Develops the knight to f3, where it supports the pawn on e5 and the pawn on d4.}
5... Qb6 {[%cal Gb6d4,Gb6b2] Piles up on d4 and eyes b2. The queen goes to b6.}
6. a3 {Prepares b4. The pawn on a3 controls b4.}
 (6. Bd3 {The Milner-Barry Gambit. Develops the bishop to d3, where it controls e4. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
6... cxd4 {Takes the pawn on d4; White will want to recapture.}
7. cxd4 {Recaptures on d4, restoring the material balance.}
7... Bd7 {Prepares ...Nxd4 and avoids Bb5+. Develops the bishop to d7, where it supports the pawn on e6 and the knight on c6.}
8. O-O {Gambits the d4 pawn. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
8... Nxd4 {Accepts. Takes the pawn on d4; White will want to recapture.}
9. Nxd4 {Recaptures on d4, restoring the material balance.}
9... Qxd4 {Recaptures on d4, restoring the material balance.}
10. Nc3 {Develops with compensation. The knight on c3 controls e4 and eyes the pawn on d5.}
)
6... c4 {[%csl Gc4] Locks the queenside to stop b4. The pawn on c4 controls b3 and d3. It also opens a line for the bishop on f8.}
7. Nbd2 {Develops the knight to d2, where it controls e4. Black's last move put a pawn on c4, which this now pressures.}
7... Na5 {[%cal Ga5b3] Eyes b3. The knight goes to a5.} *

[Event "French: Winawer"]

{The Winawer (3...Bb4) pins the knight and often gives up the bishop pair to damage White's structure.}
1. e4 {Claims the centre: the pawn on e4 controls d5 and f5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1 and the bishop on f1.}
1... e6 {French. Supports the centre: the pawn on e6 controls d5 and f5. It also opens a line for the queen on d8 and the bishop on f8.}
2. d4 {Claims the centre: the pawn on d4 controls c5 and e5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1 and the queen on d1.}
2... d5 {Challenges e4. Claims the centre: the pawn on d5 controls c4 and eyes the pawn on e4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
3. Nc3 {Defends e4. Develops the knight to c3, where it supports the pawn on e4 and eyes the pawn on d5. Black's last move put a pawn on d5, which this now pressures.}
3... Bb4 {[%cal Gb4c3] The Winawer: pins the knight. Develops the bishop to b4, where it controls c5 and d6. White's last move put a knight on c3, which this now pressures.}
4. e5 {Gains space. Claims the centre: the pawn on e5 controls d6 and f6.}
4... c5 {Hits d4. Supports the centre: the pawn on c5 supports the bishop on b4 and eyes the pawn on d4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
5. a3 {Asks the bishop. The pawn on a3 eyes the bishop on b4.}
5... Bxc3+ {Gives up the bishop pair. The bishop on c3 eyes the pawn on d4 and the pawn on b2. It is check, so the reply is forced.}
6. bxc3 {Doubled pawns. Recaptures on c3, restoring the material balance.}
6... Ne7 {Develops, ready to meet Qg4. The knight on e7 supports the pawn on d5. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
7. Qg4 {[%cal Gg4g7] Hits g7. The queen goes to g4 and controls e4 and supports the pawn on d4. It attacks the pawn on g7, which is undefended.}
 (7. Nf3 {The positional approach. Develops the knight to f3, where it supports the pawn on e5 and the pawn on d4.}
7... Qa5 {[%cal Ga5c3] Pins the c3 pawn. The queen goes to a5. It attacks the pawn on c3, which is undefended.}
8. Bd2 {Unpins. Develops the bishop to d2, where it controls e3 and f4.}
8... Nbc6 {Develops the knight to c6, where it eyes the pawn on d4 and the pawn on e5.}
9. Be2 {Develops the bishop to e2, where it controls d3 and supports the knight on f3. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
)
7... Qc7 {Counterattacks. The queen goes to c7 and eyes the pawn on e5.}
8. Qxg7 {Takes the pawn on g7, and it cannot be taken back at once.}
8... Rg8 {Hits the queen. Moves the rook out of attack to g8. It attacks the queen on g7, which is undefended.}
9. Qxh7 {Takes the pawn on h7, and it cannot be taken back at once.}
9... cxd4 {Counterattack in the centre. Takes the pawn on d4; White will want to recapture.}
10. Ne2 {Develops the knight to e2, where it eyes the pawn on d4. That pawn is currently undefended.}
10... Nbc6 {Develops the knight to c6, where it supports the pawn on d4 and eyes the pawn on e5. That pawn is currently undefended.}
11. f4 {Protects e5. Supports the centre: the pawn on f4 controls g5 and supports the pawn on e5.} *

[Event "French: Tarrasch & Exchange"]

{Against 3.Nd2 Black plays ...c5. Against the Exchange, develop actively.}
1. e4 {Claims the centre: the pawn on e4 controls d5 and f5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1 and the bishop on f1.}
1... e6 {French. Supports the centre: the pawn on e6 controls d5 and f5. It also opens a line for the queen on d8 and the bishop on f8.}
2. d4 {Claims the centre: the pawn on d4 controls c5 and e5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1 and the queen on d1.}
2... d5 {Challenges. Claims the centre: the pawn on d5 controls c4 and eyes the pawn on e4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
3. Nd2 {The Tarrasch. Develops the knight to d2, where it supports the pawn on e4.}
 (3. exd5 {The Exchange. Takes the pawn on d5; Black will want to recapture.}
3... exd5 {Recaptures; the c8-bishop is free. Recaptures on d5, restoring the material balance.}
4. Nf3 {Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and supports the pawn on d4.}
4... Nf6 {Develops the knight to f6, where it controls e4 and supports the pawn on d5.}
5. Bd3 {Develops the bishop to d3, where it controls e4. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
5... Bd6 {Develops the bishop to d6, where it controls e5. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
6. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
)
3... c5 {[%cal Gc5d4] Hits d4. Supports the centre: the pawn on c5 controls b4 and eyes the pawn on d4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
4. exd5 {Takes the pawn on d5; Black will want to recapture.}
4... Qxd5 {Recaptures on d5, restoring the material balance.}
5. Ngf3 {Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and supports the pawn on d4.}
5... cxd4 {Takes the pawn on d4; White will want to recapture.}
6. Bc4 {[%cal Gc4d5] Gains time on the queen. Develops the bishop to c4, where it eyes the queen on d5. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
6... Qd6 {Moves the queen out of attack to d6 and controls e5 and d5 and supports the pawn on d4.}
7. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7... Nf6 {Develops the knight to f6, where it controls e4 and d5.}
8. Nb3 {Hunts d4. The knight goes to b3 and eyes the pawn on d4.}
8... Nc6 {Develops the knight to c6, where it controls e5 and supports the pawn on d4.}
9. Nbxd4 {Takes the pawn on d4; Black will want to recapture.}
9... a6 {Stops Nb5. The pawn on a6 controls b5.} *
